# Keynote Demo Invariants

This app is a **live conference-stage demo**. Any change must keep the upload → preview → generating → briefing flow working end-to-end without regressions. The following files and values are effectively frozen.

## Frozen files — do not edit unless explicitly asked

- `src/lib/briefingSchema.js` — the JSON contract between Claude and the UI
- `src/prompts/weeklyBriefing.js` — system + user prompts (already tuned)
- `src/demo/fixture.js` — bundled fixture briefing used by `?demo=seed`
- `public/sample-data/` — rehearsal CSVs
- `public/logo.png` — used by the PDF exporter

## Frozen values

- Model: `MODEL = 'claude-sonnet-4-6'` in `src/lib/anthropic.js`. Do not change, upgrade, or swap providers.
- `dangerouslyAllowBrowser: true` on the Anthropic client — required (no backend).
- `cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' }` on the system prompt block — keeps token cost low.
- Env var name: `VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. Do not rename.

## Demo-safety guarantees

- Keep the `catch` branch in `handleGenerate` (`src/App.jsx`) that falls back to `loadBriefing()` when the API fails.
- Keep the `?demo=seed` / `?demo=cached` `useEffect` in `src/App.jsx` intact — these are the keynote fallbacks.
- Keep the `stop_reason === 'max_tokens'` guard in `src/lib/anthropic.js` so truncated JSON throws a clear error instead of a JSON parse crash.
- Do not remove the `isCached` badge logic in `BriefingView` — the speaker relies on it visually.

## Stack constraints

- Language is **JavaScript with JSX**. Do not migrate to TypeScript.
- Styling is **Tailwind only**. No inline `style={}` objects beyond what already exists, no new CSS files, no CSS-in-JS libraries.
- No new npm dependencies without explicit approval. `partial-json` is already installed and may be used.
- No backend, no serverless routes, no proxy — the app is a pure Vite SPA calling Anthropic directly.
- React 19 + Vite 8. Do not pin or downgrade.
- Existing Spanish localization is a demo veneer. New incremental UI copy can be English-only unless the user explicitly asks for Spanish; `useStrings` falls back to English for missing locale keys.

## Code hygiene

- Keep files under 300 lines. New logic goes in new files under `src/lib/`, `src/hooks/`, or `src/components/`.
- New components must be functional components with hooks. No class components.
- Never rename an exported symbol without updating every call site in the same change.
- Do not add narrating comments (`// set the state`). Comments should explain intent, trade-offs, or constraints only.
- Reuse existing primitives: `SectionCard`, `HeroMetric`, `useStrings`, the `formatMoney`/`formatInt`/`formatPct` helpers, and the Tailwind tokens in `tailwind.config.js` (`charcoal`, `cream`, `emerald-*`, `gold-*`, `danger`, `muted`).

## Before finishing any change

- Run `npm run build` and make sure it succeeds.
- Do not introduce new ESLint errors beyond the pre-existing `motion`-unused-var noise.
